{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_three_testing_layers", "label": "The three testing layers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Unit tests of one actor with TestKit and TestProbe, time-deterministic tests with ManualScheduler, and distributed scenarios with MultiNodeSpec or ParallelMultiNodeSpec."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_wait_on_state_not_elapsed_time", "label": "Wait on state, not on elapsed time", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A fixed sleep encodes one machine on one day and reports a late value as a wrong one; polling the observable returns after one interval and turns the timeout into a failure budget rather than an expected duration. Wait on the strongest condition the test can observe - a proxy a half-finished step already satisfies is worse than the sleep it replaced."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_awaitcondition", "label": "awaitCondition helper", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The repository's shared polling helper (tests/util/AwaitCondition.ts): returns as soon as the condition holds, and its label is what a failure reports."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_fixed_sleep_exceptions", "label": "When a fixed sleep is still right", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An absence you can only give a window to, a duration that is itself the assertion, a scenario that needs a particular interleaving, or a warm-up nothing asserts on - and the comment should say which, because a sleep with a reason is documentation and one without is a bet."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_dont_test_the_framework", "label": "Don't test the framework itself", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asserting that tell delivers passes even when the framework is broken in ways that matter, so tests should target the actor's own behaviour."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_three_testing_layers", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_testkit_testkit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_three_testing_layers", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_test_probe_testprobe", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_three_testing_layers", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_manual_scheduler_manualscheduler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_three_testing_layers", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_multi_node_spec_multinodespec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"s